anya: quick sync — QA found our streaming+paginator examples assume re-requesting full pages. gateway now emits mid-page resume tokens (X-Resume-Token). we should add tiny, copy-pasteable patterns for py/ts/go showing resume + bounded retry with jitter.
ravi: can take TS. will make an async iterator helper + note about detecting truncation (502 + header).
sam: i'll do Python and provide a small shared helper fn that docs can call. also will add the short paragraph in Streaming guide.
kai: i'll handle Go; compact snippet with ResumeToken in request struct and backoff.
anya: ravi, can you show a TS snippet that uses iterator.resume(token) semantics? keep it SDK-friendly.
ravi: sure, draft TS (pseudo-SDK):
```ts
const iter = client.streamPaginate('/v1/resumable')
for await (const page of iter) {
  for (const c of page.chunks) process.stdout.write(c.text)
  const tok = page.headers['x-resume-token']
  if (tok) iter.resume(tok)
}
```
sam: Python helper pattern (docs):
```python
from time import sleep

def drain_resumable(client, path, attempts=5):
    resume = None
    for _ in range(attempts):
        resp = client.stream_paginate(path, resume_token=resume)
        for p in resp.pages():
            for c in p.chunks: print(c.text, end='')
        resume = resp.headers.get('x-resume-token')
        if not resume:
            return
        sleep(min(3, 0.2 * (2 ** _)))
    raise RuntimeError('exhausted resume attempts')
```
kai: Go compact pseudo:
```go
req := &client.PaginateRequest{Path: "/v1/resumable"}
back := NewBackoff(200*time.Millisecond, 3*time.Second, true)
for {
  resp, err := client.StreamPaginate(ctx, req)
  if err != nil { time.Sleep(back.Next()); continue }
  io.Copy(os.Stdout, resp.Body)
  if tok := resp.Header.Get("X-Resume-Token"); tok != "" { req.ResumeToken = tok; continue }
  break
}
```
anya: suggested blurb to add under "Streaming & Pagination": "Servers may truncate long streaming responses under load. When responses include X-Resume-Token, clients should prefer server-provided resume tokens and perform bounded, jittered retries (base=200ms, max=3s, attempts=5). Avoid naive re-fetch of the entire page; resume within the page for correctness and cost savings."
ravi: i'll include a tiny helper in the TS snippet to surface detection of 502+header and bail after attempts.
